' Question: what happens, in order, when the owner starts a Grid bot?
' Explained by: ../06-runtime.md, which cites each step. Drawn by hand, high level.
@startuml 06-start
participant "StartBotCommandHandler" as UC
participant BotRunner as R
participant "GridExecutor\n(bot's worker)" as G
participant GridStartPreconditions as P
participant GridStartSequence as S
participant trading as T

UC -> UC : refuse a closed venue, an unconfirmed\nMainnet start, an unready bot
UC -> R : start(bot_id)
R -> G : start() (queued)
note over UC, R : the caller returns here; the bot's thread does the rest
G -> P : check()
P -> T : claim the symbol, open the order session,\nregister the owner budget
G -> G : DRAFT or STOPPED --start--> STARTING
G -> S : run(plan)
S -> T : place the ladder, level by level
T --> S : accepted
S -> G : ladder_ready
G -> G : STARTING --ladder_ready--> RUNNING
@enduml
